  "evidence": "TEXT_G: Leave the EU to restore sovereignty and reassert supremacy of UK law; uphold Parliament, monarchy, common law, and an independent House of Lords; stricter law and order (stronger magistrates, credible sentencing, more prison capacity); near‑zero net migration with Britishness tests and restored embarkation controls; deploy forces only in the national interest and remain in NATO; repeal the Human Rights Act; promote responsibility, family, and smaller government. TEXT_D: Strong internationalism (support EU Constitution and euro readiness); curb PM powers and create a predominantly elected second chamber with STV; Single Equality Act and hate‑crime units; allow asylum seekers to work and faster, fairer asylum; extensive care/equality policies (free personal care, abolish tuition fees, ban smoking in enclosed public places, school nutrition standards).",
  "reasoning": "The profile weights Authority and Loyalty highest, and TEXT_G centers on national sovereignty, traditional institutions, strict immigration, and law‑and‑order—directly expressing Authority/Loyalty foundations with some Proportionality. TEXT_D emphasizes Care and Equality and international integration while diluting traditional authority structures, which maps less closely to the profile’s top moral priorities.",
  "confidence": "high",
  "winner": "TEXT_G"
}
